  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Version: w_2020.2.3p1\nDescription of the bug:\nWhen people switching avatars the previous avatar they did wear still keep loading in the background, if the new avatar what they did switch to load faster due its already cached from before or smaller in file size than the previously worn avatar and the previously worn avatar finished loading in, VRChat just on my side replaces the person's avatar with the one what they did previously been wearing. At the monent the only way i can fix it if i ask the person to switch avatar once again or if i leave the world and rejoin. The main bigger problem with this is, not everyone has a super fast internet and for me its causing a huge issue when multiple people constantly keep swapping avatars and i end up not seeing anyone for a long period of time because the client just keep downloading all the avatars they swapped to for a moment...\nIts especially a problem in crowded places since the avatars almost never loading for me except maybe very few people of the crowd.\nThis wasnt a problem couple years ago, if someone switched avatar while i seen them loading, the client just ignored the previous avatar and didnt bother to keep it downloading, its should not keep downloading something thats already not being used.\nAnd this not only a problem for me but everyone else who has a slower internet due either they cant afford it or like in my case who could afford it but no one brings the fancy fiber optics into my area.\nSteps to reproduce: get a friend switch to an avatar which isnt in your cache yet, then while they still loading get them to swap to an avatar you already has in your cache, soon their avatar out of nowhere gonna get swapped with the one that was loading before.",
